    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup for 2026-07-05 is anchored by three high-upside plays, led by **Lawrence Butler** (71.52), **Taylor Ward** (71.46), and **Bryson Stott** (71.06). **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a potent combination of a 10% park boost and a massive +13% dynamic platoon edge against Eury P\u00e9rez, while **Taylor Ward** serves as our premier weapon against Lodolo, buoyed by an 18% SP skill adjustment and a significant 9% platoon advantage. **Bryson Stott** remains a must-start; despite a minor penalty for the opponent\u2019s ability to control the run game, his matchup against the soft-tossing Luinder Avila (5.01 xERA) and a massive 13% platoon boost makes him an elite option for both counting stats and efficiency. \n\nThe optimizer\u2019s most difficult decision centered on **Daulton Varsho** (54.95), who narrowly missed the starting cut in favor of **Dylan Beavers** (55.80). While **Daulton Varsho** offers intriguing speed upside against Emerson Hancock\u2014bolstered by a potential for stolen bases due to the pitcher's slow delivery\u2014the model prioritized **Dylan Beavers**' slightly higher raw floor, despite the latter's platoon disadvantage against Lodolo. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Jonathan Aranda**; **Jonathan Aranda** is a strong play today (70.44) precisely because he is projected to lead off against Peter Lambert, maximizing his exposure to run-scoring opportunities. Conversely, **Jung Hoo Lee** (59.53) remains a high-interest start due to the 100% stolen base probability projection against Tanner Gordon\u2019s delivery speed, though we must mitigate risk where \"Lineup Pending\" status is noted for key bats like **Cal Raleigh** and **Geraldo Perdomo**. As a reminder, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains sidelined, and we will continue to rely on the depth provided by **Luis Arraez**\u2014who adds stability with a 61.43 score against Gordon\u2014to navigate the remaining gaps on the roster.",
